{"parse":{"title":"kenspeckle","pageid":797816,"redirects":[],"text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"English\">English</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<p>Alteration of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/kenspeck#English\" title=\"kenspeck\">kenspeck</a></i>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Pronunciation\">Pronunciation</h3></div>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Wiktionary:International_Phonetic_Alphabet\" title=\"Wiktionary:International Phonetic Alphabet\">IPA</a><sup>(<a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:English_pronunciation\" title=\"Appendix:English pronunciation\">key</a>)</sup>:&#32;<span class=\"IPA nowrap\">/ˈkɛnspɛkəl/</span></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Adjective\">Adjective</h3></div>\n<p><span class=\"headword-line\"><strong class=\"Latn headword\" lang=\"en\">kenspeckle</strong> (<i><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#comparative\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">comparative</a></i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en comparative-form-of\" lang=\"en\">more <strong class=\"selflink\">kenspeckle</strong></b>, <i><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#superlative\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">superlative</a></i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en superlative-form-of\" lang=\"en\">most <strong class=\"selflink\">kenspeckle</strong></b>)</span>\n</p>\n<ol><li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scottish_English\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Scottish English\">Scotland</a><span class=\"ib-comma label-comma\">,</span>&#32;northern&#32;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_English\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:British English\">UK</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> Easily <a href=\"/wiki/recognize\" title=\"recognize\">recognized</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/distinctive\" title=\"distinctive\">distinctive</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/conspicuous\" title=\"conspicuous\">conspicuous</a>.\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1828</b></span>, James Hogg, <cite>Mary Burnet</cite>:</span><dl><dd><div class=\"h-quotation\"><span class=\"Latn e-quotation cited-passage\" lang=\"en\">'It &#91;the gold coin&#93; is sae bonny and sae <b>kenspeckle</b>,' said she, 'that I think I'll keep it for the sake of the giver.'</span></div></dd></dl></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Scots\">Scots</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_2\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<p>Alteration of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"sco\"><a href=\"/wiki/kenspeck#Scots\" title=\"kenspeck\">kenspeck</a></i>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Pronunciation_2\">Pronunciation</h3></div>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Wiktionary:International_Phonetic_Alphabet\" title=\"Wiktionary:International Phonetic Alphabet\">IPA</a><sup>(<a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Scots_pronunciation\" title=\"Appendix:Scots pronunciation\">key</a>)</sup>:&#32;<span class=\"IPA nowrap\">/ˈkɛnspɛkl/</span></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Adjective_2\">Adjective</h3></div>\n<p><span class=\"headword-line\"><strong class=\"Latn headword\" lang=\"sco\">kenspeckle</strong> (<i><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#comparative\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">comparative</a></i> <b class=\"Latn\" lang=\"sco\"><a href=\"/wiki/mair#Scots\" title=\"mair\">mair</a> kenspeckle</b>, <i><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#superlative\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">superlative</a></i> <b class=\"Latn\" lang=\"sco\"><a href=\"/wiki/maist#Scots\" title=\"maist\">maist</a> kenspeckle</b>)</span>\n</p>\n<ol><li>easily-<a href=\"/wiki/recognize\" title=\"recognize\">recognized</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/distinctive\" title=\"distinctive\">distinctive</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/conspicuous\" title=\"conspicuous\">conspicuous</a></li></ol>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐web.eqiad.main‐5c5554d4b‐5xf9r\nCached time: 20260924070458\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.222 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.326 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 190/1000000\nRevision size: 639/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 6769/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 472/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 8/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.186/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 11028321/104857600 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  316.755      1 -total\n 32.13%  101.788      2 Template:m\n 30.89%   97.855      2 Template:IPA\n 30.40%   96.303      2 Template:no_deprecated_lang_param_usage\n 14.09%   44.639      1 Template:lb\n  8.24%   26.089      1 Template:sco-adj\n  7.50%   23.771      1 Template:en-adj\n  6.86%   21.714      1 Template:quote-text\n  5.39%   17.074      1 Template:head\n  2.13%    6.737      2 Template:pagename\n-->\n\n<!-- Render ID 40a34e08-b7e6-11f1-bc56-fbc717562b0a -->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key enwiktionary:pcache:797816:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20260924070458 and revision id 72762734. Rendering was triggered because: page_view\n -->\n</div>"}}